      "The Leibniz formula is a classic bridge between arctangent series and pi.",
      "The metadata should show both the slow alternating-series convergence and the sharper transformed/Machin-style context.",
      "The linked Lean separates the clean convergence-rate proof from later beta/eta-series material with remaining gaps."
    ]
